The Server-Sent Events (SSE) API enables pushing 
messages/updates from a server to the web page via HTTP connection.

A server-sent event is when a web page automatically gets messages/updates from a server.

Normally, a web page has to request data from the server, but with server-sent events, the updates 
are pushed automatically.

Examples: Facebook/Twitter updates, stock market updates, news feeds, sport results, etc.

